In the circle with centre $O$, chords $AB$ and $CD$ are equal and $\angle AOB=64^{\circ}$. Find $\angle COD$. If instead $\angle AOB=\angle COD$ and $CD=4.8$ m, find $AB$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (122:2); \coordinate (B) at (58:2); \coordinate (C) at (238:2); \coordinate (D) at (302:2);
\draw (O) circle (2); \draw (A)--(B) (C)--(D); \draw (A)--(O)--(B) (C)--(O)--(D);
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt); \node[left] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$}; \node[above right] at (B) {$B$}; \node[below left] at (C) {$C$}; \node[below right] at (D) {$D$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In the circle with centre $O$, $OE\perp AB$ and $OF\perp CD$.
a. If $AB=CD$ and $OF=6.3$ cm, find $OE$.
b. If $OE=OF$ and $AB=11$ cm, find $CD$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (-1.6,1.2); \coordinate (B) at (1.6,1.2); \coordinate (C) at (-1.6,-1.2); \coordinate (D) at (1.6,-1.2); \coordinate (E) at (0,1.2); \coordinate (F) at (0,-1.2);
\draw (O) circle (2); \draw (A)--(B) (C)--(D) (E)--(O)--(F);
\draw (-0.2,1.2)--(-0.2,1)--(0,1); \draw (0.2,-1.2)--(0.2,-1)--(0,-1);
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt); \node[right] at (O) {$O$};
\node[above left] at (A) {$A$}; \node[above right] at (B) {$B$}; \node[below left] at (C) {$C$}; \node[below right] at (D) {$D$}; \node[above] at (E) {$E$}; \node[below] at (F) {$F$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circle has centre $O$. The perpendicular $OM$ meets chord $AB$ at $M$. Given $AB=18$ cm and $\angle AOB=112^{\circ}$, find $AM$ and $\angle AOM$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (146:2); \coordinate (B) at (34:2); \coordinate (M) at (0,{2*sin(34)});
\draw (O) circle (2); \draw (A)--(B) (A)--(O)--(B) (O)--(M);
\draw (0,{2*sin(34)-0.2})--(-0.2,{2*sin(34)-0.2})--(-0.2,{2*sin(34)});
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt); \node[below] at (O) {$O$}; \node[above left] at (A) {$A$}; \node[above right] at (B) {$B$}; \node[above] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

In a circle with centre $O$, $M$ lies on chord $AB$, which is not a diameter.
a. If $M$ is the midpoint of $AB$, find $\angle OMB$.
b. If instead $\angle AOM=\angle BOM$, prove that $\angle OMB=90^{\circ}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (-1.6,1.2); \coordinate (B) at (1.6,1.2); \coordinate (M) at (0,1.2);
\draw (O) circle (2); \draw (A)--(B) (A)--(O)--(B) (O)--(M);
\fill (O) circle (1.2pt); \node[below] at (O) {$O$}; \node[above left] at (A) {$A$}; \node[above right] at (B) {$B$}; \node[above] at (M) {$M$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A circle has centre $O$ and radius $OA=20$ cm. Chord $AB=32$ cm, and $OM\perp AB$ at $M$. Find $OM$ using Pythagoras' theorem.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0); \coordinate (A) at (-1.6,-1.2); \coordinate (B) at (1.6,-1.2); \coordinate (M) at (0,-1.2);
